      "table_id": "Table I",
      "description": "Means of judgments by 10 Os and medians of their standard deviations for judged slant as a function of texture type (regular, irregular), physical slant equivalent (10°, 22°, 30°, 45°), and direction of density increase (upward, downward).",
      "key_stats": [
        "Med.SD values range from 5.64 to 12.19"
      ],
      "n_findings_extracted_from": 5
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The translucent plexiglass projection screen had its own texture with a contradictory gradient, potentially affecting results.",
    "The absence of differential blur in the projected image (due to being equally in focus on a frontal screen) contradicted the texture-density gradient, favoring a perception of zero slant for the screen itself.",
    "The experimental setup (e.g., hole-screen slant, residual head-motion) contributed to a constant error, causing judged slants to be consistently biased towards a frontal surface.",
    "The reproduction method itself had a constant error, with the mean judgment of objective vertical being 4.1° forward (ceilingwise) relative to the objective vertical.",
    "Some participants reported deliberately using explicit cues (size of elements, density, linear perspective) to make judgments, raising questions about the role of inferences versus immediate impressions."
  ],
